00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.920
Significant insider purchases can serve as an alignment signal for individual investors.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.380
They prompt deeper due diligence on the name rather than automatic buying.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:03.200
Today's reported chief executive officer investment of over $1 million in an energy stock yielding

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:09.260
3.3% highlights this tactic in action. The strategy involves screening regulatory

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:14.900
filings for purchases that represent meaningful skin in the game relative to the executive's total

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.080
compensation. Then cross-check metrics such as free cash flow, price to earnings relative to

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.420
sector peers, and revenue growth trends before allocating. This approach is especially relevant

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.920
in the current environment of fluid geopolitical developments and mixed sector momentum where

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:35.260
management confidence can precede institutional re-rating. Historically, the tactic has generated

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:40.720
outperformance in resource and yield sensitive sectors during recovery phases, though risks include

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.660
insiders being too early or facing personal liquidity needs unrelated to company prospects.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:51.280
Canadian investors can set alerts on Toronto Stock Exchange listed names via free platforms.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:58.580
Cap any single name at 5% of the portfolio and pair with stop losses 8-12% below entry to manage

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:04.280
downside. This same discipline around alignment and risk shows up when we design the overall portfolio

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:10.700
itself. Imagine you constructed a $100,000 portfolio last month with 80% in a core global

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:18.280
equity exchange traded fund like XEQT during the 5% geopolitical dip and 20% in a thematic satellite

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:25.820
exchange traded fund focused on clean energy. Your core order filled at net asset value with a 0.20%

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:32.360
management expense ratio. The satellite filled with a 0.45% management expense ratio and saw its

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:39.520
allocation drift to 26% after a sharp 11% sector rally. The core delivered broad exposure across

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:46.480
8,000 plus holdings with 14% annualized volatility and 0.92 correlation to the Toronto Stock Exchange,

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:53.820
anchoring the portfolio. The satellite's 28% volatility and 0.55 correlation provided true

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:59.200
non-overlapping upside that added 2.1% to overall return despite higher fees.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:07.340
The core satellite mechanism typically sets 70-80% in low cost, broad index exchange traded funds,

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:14.100
such as XEQT, VTI and VXUS for stability and tax-efficient buy and hold behavior.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:21.080
It reserves 20-30% for 2-4 tactical thematic or sector exchange traded funds that are rebalanced

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:26.420
every six months or when any satellite deviates more than 5% from target weight. Rebalancing

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:32.860
frequency matters because a satellite that runs from 10% to 18% of the portfolio can unintentionally

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:38.120
dominate risk without adding the intended alpha. Professionals always calculate the marginal

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:43.500
contribution to portfolio volatility before adding a satellite. If it pushes total draw-down

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:48.600
risk above 18% in a stress test, they reject the position regardless of the themes appeal.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.760
The biggest mistake with core satellite is treating underperforming satellites like

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:57.780
permanent core holdings and letting them drift indefinitely. Instead, always define success metrics

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:03.260
upfront such as exit if the satellite underperforms its sector benchmark by more than 10% over

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:08.320
two consecutive quarters. The same patience and rules based thinking that governs core satellite

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:15.320
portfolios explains why we are in observation mode today. No pick today as waste management 10% drop

